<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The launcher icon's foreground, and — on this phone — the splash icon too.

     Same mark as `features/shared/lotus_mark.dart`, refitted to the adaptive-icon
     canvas: 108 units, of which only the middle 66 are reliably visible once a
     launcher applies its mask. The mark is 60 across, so it clears that with room.

     The stroke is 2.2 rather than the 1.9 the app draws, because this is read at 48dp
     on a home screen and not at 74dp on a splash — a contour that is correct at one
     size disappears at the other.

     Reused as `monochrome`, which is the whole argument for stroke art here: a themed
     icon is tinted by the system, and a silhouette would have had to be drawn twice. -->
